From b05bffd8f2a6d6cca21522041214794c1ea588e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: benjamin <benjamin.hien@web.de>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 03:35:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Phase 5 slice 5A: port runways behind
 PHOTONIC_ROUTER_PORT_RUNWAYS=1

Every cardinal port without a fan-out stub gets a runway: a static stub
from the port centre onto the cell-centre lattice (0.5 um straight
lead-in, two shallow arcs of the bend radius for the sub-cell lateral
residue, straight to the first cell centre at or beyond the arcs). The
anchor is that cell centre with the port's heading; the search starts and
ends there as it does for the fan-out stubs, and the realized route is
stub + search path, so endpoint correction has nothing to move. Nets whose
ports are closer than their two runways (the pre-placed crossing grids'
tile links) keep the old path; the crossing structures' entry-tile probe
(static_fanout_anchors_um) reports fan-out anchors only.

Switch off: gate exact, 711 Python tests. Switch on, nine cells: crossings
identical, 0 verifier errors, Benes +0.5-0.6 % length, ADEPT 8x8 baseline
-0.24 %, c1 -0.04 %, c2 +0.52 %; arcs per net 2.2 -> 6.6 (Benes 8x8) and
2.9 -> 5.1 (ADEPT 8x8). Decision by the 27-cell table and the owner.

